From 635ee0928725ad27c08422d79bbfa7bf50888bf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:36:08 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] [VideoPlayer] Let a stop interrupt the demuxer probe of any
 input stream

Only CDVDInputStreamFFmpeg remembered an abort, so CDVDDemuxFFmpeg's
interrupt callback could stop the probe of streams that FFmpeg opens
itself (such as HLS, RTSP, RTMP, UDP, and PVR channels with
inputstream=inputstream.ffmpeg) but nothing else. A stop while any
other input was being probed, such as a local, smb, nfs or http file
or a PVR stream, waited for the probe to finish, up to the 30 s open
timeout, with the app thread blocked in StopThread(): 14 s for a
70 KB/s http source here, 30 s at 25 KB/s.

Keep the flag in CDVDInputStream, set it in Abort() and have the demuxer
check it for every input. CDVDInputStreamBluray uses it in place of its
own, and CInputStreamMultiSource's override calls the base first. The
flag is never cleared: an input stream is opened once and not reused.

An interrupted probe can still succeed, as FFmpeg keeps the streams it
already has parameters for, so this relies on the m_bStop check in
OpenStream() from #30283 to not go on and open them. The probe can now
end before StopThread() sets m_bStop, so CloseFile() sets it first,
before it aborts anything. A read already in flight still blocks until
it returns; CFileCache and CCurlFile have no abort of their own.

Assisted-by: Claude
(cherry picked from commit 08f8fb1976fd5d1bb2b1d6e56015d89d653c05a6)
